{
  "_doc": [
    "Level modules -> hazard tokens.",
    "",
    "A PvZ2 level is a LevelDefinition plus a list of MODULES, and the modules",
    "are where every hazard lives: the tide, the wind, the graves, the conveyor.",
    "The extractor collects every objclass appearing anywhere inside a level's",
    "module list and maps it through this table.",
    "",
    "`module_tokens` keys are matched CASE-INSENSITIVELY as SUBSTRINGS of the",
    "objclass, so 'gravestone' catches GravestoneModuleProperties and",
    "SpawnGravestoneWaveActionProps alike. Longest key wins on a tie.",
    "",
    "`world_tokens` is the fallback for a level whose modules we could not read",
    "-- and, today, the ONLY source of hazard data, because the pipeline can run",
    "with no game checkout. It is per-world and deliberately conservative: it",
    "names only what every level of that world plainly has. When a checkout is",
    "present the module scan supersedes it per level, and the built record says",
    "which source each token came from.",
    "",
    "`unmapped` is written back by the extractor with every objclass it saw and",
    "had no entry for, so extending this file is a matter of reading that list",
    "rather than guessing.",
    "",
    "`ignore` is matched the same way as module_tokens and drops a module from the unmapped report entirely. It holds the ~100 objclasses that are level PLUMBING rather than hazards -- stages, mowers, intros, win conditions, seed banks, the wave manager itself. Without it the unmapped list is mostly noise and stops being the thing you read to extend this file."
  ],
